{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Designing a reliable file backup system requires a shift in mindset from \"backing up\" (the act of copying data) to \"restoring\" (the act of recovering data). A backup is only successful if the restoration process works.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive architectural guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Backup Strategies: Full vs. Incremental\nA reliable system rarely relies on a single method; it uses a hybrid approach to balance storage efficiency with recovery speed.\n\n#### Full Backups\nA full backup copies all selected files and folders.\n*   **Pros:** Simplest to restore;"},"logprobs":{"content":[{"id":47789,"token":"Design","bytes":[68,101,115,105,103,110],"logprob":-0.5337351560592651,"top_logprobs":[{"id":47789,"token":"Design","bytes":[68,101,115,105,103,110],"logprob":-0.5337351560592651},{"id":1035,"token":"#","bytes":[35],"logprob":-1.7176035642623901},{"id":1784,"token":"The","bytes":[84,104,101],"logprob":-2.7649173736572266},{"id":1065,"token":"A","bytes":[65],"logprob":-3.2603626251220703},{"id":1595,"token":"###","bytes":[35,35,35],"logprob":-3.4463558197021484}]},{"id":1302,"token":"ing","bytes":[105,110,103],"logprob":-1.180178969661938e-05,"top_logprobs":[{"id":1302,"token":"ing","bytes":[105,110,103],"logprob":-1.180178969661938e-05},{"id":1261,"token":" a","bytes":[32,97],"logprob":-11.837570190429688},{"id":1307,"token":" of","bytes":[32,111,102],"logprob":-13.069393157958984},{"id":1010,"token":"\n","bytes":[10],"logprob":-14.585521697998047},{"id":1395,"token":" is","bytes":[32,105,115],"logprob":-15.130252838134766}]},{"id":1261,"token":" a","bytes":[32,97],"logprob":-2.837221290974412e-05,"top_logprobs":[{"id":1261,"token":" a","bytes":[32,97],"logprob":-2.837221290974412e-05},{"id":1321,"token":" and","bytes":[32,97,110,100],"logprob":-11.212419509887695},{"id":1420,"token":" an","bytes":[32,97,110],"logprob":-11